							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1026.msg10256#msg10256"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1026.msg10256#msg10256">Re: Not much but maybe good for a spark.</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #27 on:</b> August 19, 2004, 03:28:26 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1026.msg10159#msg10159">Quote from: Vanden RN on August 17, 2004, 04:04:44 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><br /><br />Hell, if that&#039;s as harsh as it gets on internal Hegemony communications, I&#039;d think Conviction members would feel pretty good about their relationship/rivalry with Hegemony.  No bashing about Conviction&#039;s people/abilities.  No direct threats made regarding Conviction.  No subversive tactics mentioned.  Some embellishment favoring Hegemony, but mostly just sounds more like a troop rally in case server rumors turn out to be true.<br /><br /><br /></div><br />Actually Vanden, that&#039;s pretty much the case.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
